# A release snapshot is `git archive HEAD`, and the builder compiles inside that
# extracted tarball: no `.git` directory, and Stado's build environment carries
# no revision (WISENT_SOURCE_DIR, WISENT_OUTPUT_DIR, WISENT_INPUTS_DIR,
# WISENT_PRODUCT, WISENT_VERSION, WISENT_PLATFORM is the whole list). So the
# revision has to travel inside the archive, and `export-subst` is git's own way
# to put it there: `.release-commit` holds `$Format:%H$` in the working tree and
# the 40-hex commit in every archive taken of it.
#
# Without this the published binary reported `commit: null`, which is why a host
# could not tell a managed binary from one somebody built by hand.
.release-commit export-subst
